WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.069
All together: Hi, we’re Marc, Aya, Júlia and Biel.

2
00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:08.191
Our group chose St Lucia’s Day, and we’d like to propose a Lucia Morning at our school.

3
00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:14.429
Marc: St Lucia’s Day is celebrated in Sweden on the thirteenth of December.

4
00:00:14.729 --> 00:00:21.796
Lucy was a young Christian woman who lived in Sicily about 1,700 years ago.

5
00:00:22.096 --> 00:00:31.917
In the old calendar, the thirteenth of December used to be the longest night of the year in Sweden, and people used to stay awake with candles and food.

6
00:00:32.217 --> 00:00:37.832
Today, for the people who celebrate it, Lucia means light and hope in the darkest season.

7
00:00:38.132 --> 00:00:43.392
It belongs at our school because it brings everyone together on a dark winter morning.

8
00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:48.508
Aya: I’m Aya, and I’m going to compare Lucia with a celebration here.

9
00:00:48.808 --> 00:00:55.924
In Catalonia, we celebrate Santa Llúcia on the same day, and both celebrations remember the same saint.

10
00:00:56.224 --> 00:00:59.592
In both places, it’s the start of the Christmas season.

11
00:00:59.892 --> 00:01:02.166
However, the customs are quite different.

12
00:01:02.466 --> 00:01:12.983
In Sweden, children walk in a procession and sing in the early morning, while here people go to the Santa Llúcia fair in Barcelona to buy figures for the nativity scene.

13
00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:15.169
Júlia: I’m Júlia.

14
00:01:15.469 --> 00:01:21.551
Our Lucia Morning will take place on Friday the eleventh of December, because the thirteenth is a Sunday.

15
00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:26.464
It’s going to start at nine o’clock in the school hall with a short procession and a song.

16
00:01:26.764 --> 00:01:34.290
From half past nine to half past ten, there will be three workshops: paper stars, Lucia crowns and a few Swedish words.

17
00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:42.360
At break time, we’re going to share saffron buns and hot chocolate, like a Swedish “fika”, and at eleven we’ll finish with a quiz.

18
00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:44.402
Biel: I’m Biel.

19
00:01:44.702 --> 00:01:51.757
Marc and Aya are going to organise the procession, Júlia will run the workshops, and I’ll make the buns with the cooking club.

20
00:01:52.057 --> 00:01:55.335
We need white T-shirts, battery candles, paper and saffron.

21
00:01:55.635 --> 00:02:00.913
Anyone can take part as Lucia or as a helper, and we’ll make buns without gluten too.

22
00:02:01.213 --> 00:02:04.365
There’s a stereotype that Lucia is always a blond girl.

23
00:02:04.665 --> 00:02:07.819
It’s unfair, because people in Sweden look very different.

24
00:02:08.119 --> 00:02:11.801
That’s why we’ll choose our Lucia by lottery from all the volunteers.

25
00:02:12.101 --> 00:02:13.186
Thank you for listening!
